WEBVTT

00:00.550 --> 00:03.885
This demo connects Cosmos and Instant LiDAR in one workflow.

00:05.150 --> 00:09.368
First, the Cosmos world model turns control signals into video and
LiDAR.

00:10.400 --> 00:14.616
Instant LiDAR then reconstructs a 3D scene from these generated
point clouds.

00:17.250 --> 00:22.524
The result is a reusable Gaussian asset, built in about fifty-one
seconds without per-scene training.

00:25.300 --> 00:28.269
With the asset ready, we can render along different paths.

00:30.200 --> 00:34.190
Here, we compare the original path with a path shifted three meters
to the left.

00:39.200 --> 00:44.462
Next, we keep both paths and switch between thirty-two, sixty-four,
and one hundred twenty-eight beams.

00:49.100 --> 00:53.073
These views all come from the same asset, ready to reuse in
simulation.

00:56.650 --> 01:04.521
This workflow shows how Instant LiDAR and the Cosmos world model
turn control signals into reusable simulation assets through fast 3D
reconstruction.
